    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "ATR 42\nTS\nTRANS STATES\nTS) AIRLINES.\nSAFETY ON BOARD\n• Passengers must comply with safety instruc-\ntions of crewmembers, signs and all placards.\n• Know the location and operation of all emergency\nequipment and exits.\n• Keep your seatbelt on at all times while seated.\n• No smoking at any time on board this aircraft.\n• Please do not remove this card from the aircraft.\nTSA ATR42-1 Rev: 6/25/99",
      "Flotation\ncushion\n1\n2\nWater\nevacuation\nroutes\nEmergency\nequipment\n2\n3\nAim at base of fire\nCopyright © 1992, 1999. Aero Safety Graphics Inc. All Rights Reserved. Printed in USA (800) 376-4622 Fax: (425) 957-0932\n2002.127.562",
      "Bracing\npositions\nA child occupying an approved device should be braced according to manufacturers instructions.\nAssess outside conditions\nRear facing seats only!\nOPEN\nIf thick smoke, fire, metal debris or obstructions are visible, or if the water level is above the sill of an exit, DO NOT OPEN. Redirect passengers to other usable exits.\nEmergency exits\nKnow the location and\noperation of all exits.\nEmergency exit routes\nB\nA\nFollow lights to exits\nBeware of propeller\nA\nEXIT\nEmergency 1\noxygen\nCrew will hand masks out\nOK...\nForward\nemergency\nexits\nA\nPull handle in\nAft\nemergency\nexit\nB\nPull handle in and turn counter-clockwise\n2\nAft stairs\nexit\nC\nPull handle up\nDOOR WEIGHT: 29 Ibs\n3\nBeware of\npropellers.\nTurn window on side and discard outside\nPush door out to the left\nPush stairs out"
    ],
